{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS A STATEMENT THAT RAISES SEVERAL QUESTIONS ABOUT THE NATURE OF AUTHORITY AND MORALITY. ON ONE HAND, IT CAN BE ARGUED THAT THIS SENTENCE ENCOURAGES CRITICAL THINKING AND MORAL AUTONOMY, AS IT SUGGESTS THAT INDIVIDUALS SHOULD NOT BLINDLY FOLLOW LAWS THAT THEY DEEM TO BE UNJUST. HOWEVER, ON THE OTHER HAND, THIS SENTENCE CAN ALSO BE SEEN AS A RECIPE FOR ANARCHY AND SOCIAL UNREST, AS IT IMPLIES THAT INDIVIDUALS HAVE THE RIGHT TO DISREGARD LAWS THAT THEY DISAGREE WITH, REGARDLESS OF THE CONSEQUENCES.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS ALSO PROBLEMATIC BECAUSE IT FAILS TO PROVIDE ANY CLEAR GUIDELINES FOR DETERMINING WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW. WHO GETS TO DECIDE WHAT LAWS ARE JUST OR UNJUST? SHOULD INDIVIDUALS BE ALLOWED TO MAKE THIS DETERMINATION BASED ON THEIR OWN PERSONAL BELIEFS AND VALUES, OR SHOULD THERE BE SOME HIGHER AUTHORITY THAT MAKES THIS DECISION? THE SENTENCE RAISES MORE QUESTIONS THAN IT ANSWERS, AND ITS SIMPLICITY BELIES THE COMPLEXITY OF THE ISSUES IT ADDRESSES. THEREFORE, IT IS A SENTENCE THAT SHOULD BE APPROACHED WITH CAUTION AND CRITICAL EVALUATION.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -7.521823135903105e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -7.152531907195225e-06}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.0007113072206266224}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.31508296728134155}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.0010349161457270384}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": -8.702239938429557e-06}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " LAW", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": 0.0}, {"to